@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+# b2s report
+
+tests-first: exempt tests only, no lib change.
+
+## Files changed
+- controller_app/test/chip_readable_test.dart (new): chip at 568x320 and 667x375, menu and TV look: exists, inside screen, >= 48 dp, label not cut (didExceedMaxLines), no thrown exception.
+- controller_app/test/connect_narrow_test.dart: `knownTopBarOverflow` removed; the 568 TV case now passes.
+- controller_app/test/connection_chip_test.dart: `if (tv) return` removed; both TV cases that now fail are marked `skip`.
+- controller_app/test/touch_targets_test.dart: the 568 TV `continue` removed; only the pad case at 568 TV is skipped (it fails).
+
+## Open (chip not readable; lib not touched)
+flutter_test's `skip` takes a bool, so the measurements are in comments and in `_knownUnreadable`, not in a skip string.
+- 568x320 menu: label "Android TV" cut (didExceedMaxLines true), chip rect (12, 4, 161.9, 52).
+- 568x320 TV: chip rect (12, 4, 47.9, 52), 35.9 dp wide (< 48). Also fails touch_targets (pad: 35.9 x 48) and connection_chip 568 TV.
+- 667x375 TV: label "Android TV" cut, chip rect (12, 4, 146.9, 52). Also fails connection_chip 667 TV.
+- 667x375 menu passes. No layout overflow exception was seen in any case (the old 12 px top-bar overflow is gone, connect_narrow passes).
+- Skipped (not deleted): 3 in chip_readable_test, 2 in connection_chip_test, 1 in touch_targets_test.
+
+## Questions
+- Skips here hide the cut label at 568 menu; the owner may want the bar fixed rather than the cases skipped.
+
+## Commit message
+m165 b2s: chip readability tests, three old skips removed
+
+New chip_readable_test checks the connection chip at 568x320 and 667x375
+in the menu and TV look. The three old TV skips are removed; the cases
+that still fail (cut label, chip under 48 dp wide) are skipped with their
+measured values as B-044 control, lib untouched.
+
+## Status row
+b2s: chip readable test added and old skips removed; open: chip cut/narrow at 568 menu, 568 TV, 667 TV (6 skipped cases).
+
+## Delete
+- none
